WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.172
- Oh, wait for me.
- Oh.

00:47.922 --> 00:49.007
[sighs]

00:52.135 --> 00:54.137
[playful music playing]

00:58.433 --> 00:59.768
[elevator operator] Doors closing.

00:59.851 --> 01:01.227
[Seok-ho] Hold the door, please.

01:01.311 --> 01:02.812
[elevator operator] Doors opening.

01:02.896 --> 01:04.022
Ah.

01:04.647 --> 01:06.357
Heading home?

01:07.400 --> 01:08.651
[elevator operator] Doors closing.

01:10.987 --> 01:11.988
[sighs]

01:13.782 --> 01:14.949
What did you get?

01:15.033 --> 01:16.659
[plastic rustles]

01:17.243 --> 01:18.745
A new faucet for the kitchen.

01:18.828 --> 01:21.164
- Mine's leaking.
- Oh.

01:21.247 --> 01:22.665
Wouldn't the landlord…

01:23.917 --> 01:26.586
Oh, hang on. You own it, don't you?

01:26.669 --> 01:29.088
Wow, that's great.

01:29.172 --> 01:31.049
Technically, it belongs to the bank.

01:31.132 --> 01:33.009
Still, if it's in your name,
that's awesome.

01:33.092 --> 01:35.553
Good for you.
[breathes deeply]

01:35.637 --> 01:37.847
You got a great job and a great place.

01:37.931 --> 01:39.474
Whoever she is, she's lucky.

01:40.016 --> 01:42.894
- Who?
- Whoever you marry one day.

01:43.812 --> 01:44.687
[scoffs]

01:47.148 --> 01:48.441
[elevator dings]

01:49.150 --> 01:51.486
[elevator operator]
Twelfth floor. Doors opening.

01:52.403 --> 01:54.197
- That's me.
- See ya. Bye.

01:58.993 --> 02:00.995
- [lock beeping]
- [elevator operator] Doors closing.

02:01.621 --> 02:02.789
Who are you?

02:04.332 --> 02:06.334
Hm? Is there something
I can help you with?

02:06.960 --> 02:08.336
You don't…

02:08.419 --> 02:09.838
My daughter lives here.

02:11.673 --> 02:12.757
[gasps]

02:12.841 --> 02:14.092
[door opens]

02:14.175 --> 02:16.052
- Uh…
- Oh?

02:17.679 --> 02:19.681
[quirky music playing]

02:25.979 --> 02:27.147
Good evening.

02:29.732 --> 02:30.900
Hello.

02:45.498 --> 02:47.208
[people] Say you will.

02:47.292 --> 02:50.211
- Say you will.
- [people cheering]

02:51.254 --> 02:52.964
[slurps]

02:54.257 --> 02:55.675
Why would they take a risk like that?

02:55.758 --> 02:59.095
That whole thing
of marriage being the end goal,

02:59.178 --> 03:00.388
it's not always right.

03:01.598 --> 03:02.891
[sighs]

03:02.974 --> 03:06.644
[cell phone buzzing]

03:06.728 --> 03:09.689
LEE SI-WOO

03:13.276 --> 03:14.193
Hey, I just finished--

03:14.277 --> 03:16.654
[Si-woo] I think you should go home
right away.

03:17.530 --> 03:18.448
Huh?

03:21.659 --> 03:24.454
To summarize and make sure I understand,

03:25.705 --> 03:27.916
all of you are living together,
because of your work?

03:27.999 --> 03:29.918
Yes. We work together. So that's why.

03:30.418 --> 03:31.711
When will you go?

03:31.794 --> 03:33.630
Uh, we'll leave…

03:34.213 --> 03:36.466
When we can go to our houses--

03:36.549 --> 03:39.177
No, just until the season's over.

03:39.260 --> 03:40.470
That's right, yeah.

03:41.721 --> 03:43.806
You'll be here the rest of the season.

03:45.183 --> 03:46.643
Several months away.

03:46.726 --> 03:48.269
- [Dong-han] Yes.
- Yeah.

03:49.896 --> 03:51.606
She's gone crazy letting not just one

03:51.689 --> 03:54.234
but two men live in her apartment
when she lives alone?

03:54.859 --> 03:58.279
Oh, the weather this time of year
is especially dangerous.

03:58.363 --> 04:01.366
And just makes sense to be able to review
and discuss it at any time, right?

04:01.449 --> 04:03.409
Yes. Yeah, it makes sense.

04:04.535 --> 04:06.871
I apologize if we alarmed you
at all, madam.

04:08.289 --> 04:09.499
Right. Okay.

04:09.582 --> 04:12.585
My daughter isn't going to be
a perky spring chicken forever,

04:12.669 --> 04:15.713
so I'm worried she must've lost her mind.

04:17.924 --> 04:19.259
[whispers]
What's a spring chicken?

04:20.093 --> 04:21.844
[whispers]
Someone who can get a husband easily.

04:22.720 --> 04:24.347
[in normal voice]
Also, I was wondering about,

04:24.430 --> 04:27.183
in the elevator,
there was a man you were talking to.

04:27.267 --> 04:29.143
How exactly does he know you?

04:29.727 --> 04:31.729
Oh, he works with us at the KMA.

04:32.230 --> 04:33.398
- Who?
- Seok-ho.

04:33.481 --> 04:35.233
Oh, of course. Seok-ho's on team two.

04:35.316 --> 04:37.318
Oh, and is he spoken for?

04:37.402 --> 04:38.903
- Oh, no, not yet.
- Yes, he's single.

04:38.987 --> 04:40.989
- His age?
- Huh?

04:41.072 --> 04:43.992
I wanna know how old that man,
your co-worker is.

04:44.075 --> 04:46.911
I think he's the same age
as Miss Jin, isn't he?

04:46.995 --> 04:48.955
- Oh.
- [Si-woo] He's not…

04:49.038 --> 04:51.332
Uh, Seok-ho is a few years older
than he looks.

04:51.416 --> 04:54.377
So he'd actually be older than Miss Jin.

04:55.753 --> 04:57.088
Uh, seven years older.

04:57.171 --> 04:58.756
- Oh.
- [nervous chuckle]

05:00.842 --> 05:04.345
Seven years? That'd be okay.

05:05.763 --> 05:07.390
- Seven years?
- [door opens]

05:11.060 --> 05:13.688
Mom, you should've told me
you were coming.

05:13.771 --> 05:16.482
How could you let these random men
into your home?

05:16.566 --> 05:18.901
You should've at least discussed it
with me first.

05:19.485 --> 05:20.695
Please. I know who they are.

05:20.778 --> 05:23.072
It's just Mr. Um
and a forecaster from team two.

05:24.532 --> 05:26.200
I knew things were off

05:26.284 --> 05:29.329
when you hurried over after I threatened
to come here and get you.

05:29.954 --> 05:32.206
I thought there must be some secret here
you've been hiding.

05:32.874 --> 05:34.167
And I…

05:35.001 --> 05:36.544
[Ha-kyung] It's just because of work.

05:36.627 --> 05:38.338
It's our busiest season
and I'm overwhelmed,

05:38.421 --> 05:39.881
because I've never done this
as a director.

05:39.964 --> 05:42.050
There's a lot on my plate,
so they're helping me out.

05:42.133 --> 05:43.217
Yeah, right.

05:43.718 --> 05:46.554
When did you start asking for help
when you're overwhelmed?

05:46.637 --> 05:49.098
You'd suffer in silence
until it killed you, I know.

05:50.308 --> 05:52.727
[sighs]
Let's not do this here. Follow me.

05:52.810 --> 05:54.479
It's too hot. Let's talk here.

05:54.562 --> 05:56.564
- Come on, we need to go. Mom!
- Huh?

05:57.774 --> 05:58.816
Ridiculous.

05:58.900 --> 06:00.693
- See you…
- Good night, ma'am.

06:22.548 --> 06:24.050
[cell phone buzzes]

06:24.133 --> 06:26.385
MOM

06:34.018 --> 06:35.269
Hey, Mom.

06:36.354 --> 06:37.855
Ugh, I know.

06:37.939 --> 06:41.150
Work came up and I had no choice,
I couldn't get away.

06:42.110 --> 06:44.487
Sorry, we'll do a belated birthday.

06:45.655 --> 06:47.156
Hm? A bag?

06:52.411 --> 06:54.330
- Did you go shopping again?
- Oh, that's--

06:54.413 --> 06:55.957
Must be nice to be so carefree.

06:56.040 --> 06:59.961
Are you saying that I'm just
thoughtlessly spending our money?

07:01.045 --> 07:02.130
If you're being rational,

07:02.839 --> 07:05.299
you wouldn't spend our money
like it's nothing.

07:09.178 --> 07:10.388
Oh, uh…

07:11.222 --> 07:12.932
Right. How did I forget it?

07:13.766 --> 07:16.394
Actually, Yu-jin picked
the bag out for you, yeah.

07:17.019 --> 07:18.646
I told you before.

07:18.729 --> 07:20.982
Yu-jin's great. She's really thoughtful.

07:21.065 --> 07:24.235
You always say she's no Ha-kyung,
like I made a mistake,

07:24.318 --> 07:26.446
but you'll see, she's wonderful.

07:30.700 --> 07:32.660
Mm. Is that so?

07:32.743 --> 07:35.329
Why don't you give her a call
and grab dinner again sometime?

07:36.038 --> 07:37.165
Mm.

07:38.541 --> 07:39.709
Mm-hm.

07:44.422 --> 07:48.217
Oh, no. Damn it. I'm such an idiot.
[sighs]

07:50.428 --> 07:55.183
[TV chatter]

08:16.496 --> 08:17.747
[sighs]

08:19.624 --> 08:20.541
[beeps]

08:23.044 --> 08:27.006
Um… Uh…
[sighs]

08:27.089 --> 08:30.468
You could've… You should've told me.

08:33.221 --> 08:34.472
About the purse.

08:36.807 --> 08:39.185
She took it when she went
to meet her friend,

08:39.268 --> 08:40.811
and everyone noticed it.

08:40.895 --> 08:43.272
She called and told me all about it.

08:43.356 --> 08:45.608
They all said she's lucky to have
a great daughter-in-law.

08:45.691 --> 08:46.692
It was a real compliment.

08:48.361 --> 08:50.112
I'm sorry for what I said

08:50.947 --> 08:51.864
the other day.

08:54.158 --> 08:55.243
Well, now you know.

08:57.411 --> 08:58.538
Also,

08:59.580 --> 09:01.249
how did you pay for the bag?

09:01.874 --> 09:04.877
We're maxed out on all our credit cards.

09:04.961 --> 09:07.964
I used my bonus,
plus a little from my emergency fund.

09:09.882 --> 09:12.885
We're so busy right now,
we don't even have time

09:12.969 --> 09:14.178
to dream about a vacation.

09:15.429 --> 09:18.182
It seemed like a better idea to use it
for the gift.

09:21.018 --> 09:22.395
Thanks for that, Yu-jin.

09:23.688 --> 09:26.440
I haven't been thinking straight
the past few days.

09:28.192 --> 09:29.360
Whatever.

09:29.443 --> 09:31.946
Oh, forgive me just this once.

09:35.866 --> 09:38.202
[groans, whines]

09:38.286 --> 09:40.246
I'm the worst. Please forgive me.

09:40.329 --> 09:42.665
[chuckles]
You want a massage?

09:42.748 --> 09:43.708
[scoffs]

09:43.791 --> 09:45.334
[laughs]

09:45.418 --> 09:47.211
I'm so sorry. I'll be better.

09:48.963 --> 09:50.548
With more people living in the apartment,

09:50.631 --> 09:52.967
the water bills and electricity bills
are going to be higher.

09:53.050 --> 09:54.760
Are they gonna be covering the difference?

09:54.844 --> 09:56.262
They're staying as my guests.

09:56.345 --> 09:57.471
Huh.

09:58.222 --> 10:01.100
You should still split it with them,
plus maintenance.

10:01.684 --> 10:03.227
Mom, I'm their boss.

10:03.311 --> 10:04.854
Yeah, so?

10:06.814 --> 10:09.275
You're so smart and so clueless
at the same time.

10:12.194 --> 10:14.530
It seems like Director Jin's mom

10:15.990 --> 10:18.909
was really interested in Mr. Shin's life.

10:18.993 --> 10:21.203
Well, it doesn't even matter.
Ha-kyung doesn't see it that way.

10:21.287 --> 10:23.998
Her mom would set her up
with anyone she can find.

10:24.915 --> 10:28.544
Seok-ho is a little boring, isn't he?

10:28.628 --> 10:31.881
It's not like he's a perfect person,
I mean, no one is,

10:31.964 --> 10:35.426
but he seems difficult to live with too.

10:36.052 --> 10:38.846
He'd probably be a good husband,
though, wouldn't he?

10:41.641 --> 10:45.019
Well, even if he was, there's no way
he could ever date Ha-kyung.

10:46.020 --> 10:48.397
Seok-ho's not even… He and Director Jin,

10:48.898 --> 10:50.983
I think they're way too different
to be together.

10:51.567 --> 10:53.361
Different hobbies,
different personalities…

10:53.444 --> 10:55.780
And the chemistry is non-existent.
They don't have any.

10:55.863 --> 10:57.490
Hey.

10:58.658 --> 11:01.452
Stranger things have happened, you know?

11:01.535 --> 11:05.456
Romance is completely unpredictable,
you'll never know what will happen.

11:05.539 --> 11:07.625
Especially if they're working together
every day.

11:08.167 --> 11:09.168
Hey.

11:09.669 --> 11:14.131
You never know. Just you wait.

11:17.218 --> 11:18.052
[chuckles]

11:20.638 --> 11:21.597
[snickers]

11:24.850 --> 11:25.684
[sighs]

11:28.229 --> 11:29.063
[groans]

11:35.736 --> 11:36.821
So,

11:37.405 --> 11:40.950
the fellow that lives above you
works for the KMA?

11:41.575 --> 11:43.994
- The Assistant Director?
- He's what?

11:45.287 --> 11:48.999
I was thinking he seems really nice.
He seems nice and takes care of himself.

11:49.083 --> 11:50.709
- Right?
- Okay, and?

11:50.793 --> 11:52.503
- It's here.
- Well, he…

11:52.586 --> 11:55.047
He seems like he'd be great for you.

11:55.131 --> 11:57.466
And I want you to consider him,
just for a second.

11:57.550 --> 11:59.468
You could get to know him outside of work.

11:59.552 --> 12:01.720
I mean, who knows, huh? Consider it.

12:01.804 --> 12:03.722
Thank you. Get home safe, huh?

12:08.018 --> 12:09.979
He's the Assistant Director?

12:11.605 --> 12:13.607
Seven years isn't that bad.

12:13.691 --> 12:16.026
[lock beeping]

12:16.110 --> 12:17.695
- [lock chimes]
- [door opens]

12:19.738 --> 12:21.740
- [door closes]
- [lock chimes]

12:33.002 --> 12:34.920
Did you get your mom a cab?

12:36.589 --> 12:37.631
Mm-hm.

12:40.759 --> 12:42.094
Si-woo, oppa…

12:42.803 --> 12:43.888
doesn't want marriage.

12:46.223 --> 12:49.977
He has no intention of marrying anyone.

12:53.606 --> 12:57.735
Ha-kyung doesn't date just anybody,
unless there's a chance of marriage.

13:00.196 --> 13:01.989
You are aware of that, right?

13:08.412 --> 13:10.831
- Maybe we should get… a drink?
- You want a beer?

13:10.915 --> 13:13.000
[both chuckle]

13:14.418 --> 13:16.003
- Let's do it.
- Okay.

13:16.086 --> 13:17.129
[chuckles]

13:28.849 --> 13:30.935
So I was chatting with Miss Chae.

13:32.728 --> 13:34.897
And she said you don't believe
in marriage.

13:37.024 --> 13:37.858
Yeah.

13:44.782 --> 13:46.534
Would you mind explaining that more?

13:47.368 --> 13:49.328
It's just not something I'd ever want.

13:50.037 --> 13:53.374
I don't really think that you have
to get married to prove you're in love.

13:56.085 --> 13:58.587
And then you're responsible
for your in-laws,

13:58.671 --> 14:00.130
you owe everyone more.

14:01.298 --> 14:04.468
And I wouldn't want to weigh down
the person I love

14:05.886 --> 14:07.263
with my problems.

14:13.936 --> 14:17.273
So you think a larger family
has to be a burden?

14:17.856 --> 14:19.149
You've met my father.

14:22.486 --> 14:26.156
It just seems easiest to decide
I'll never do it.

14:32.329 --> 14:33.372
You're mad, aren't you?

14:34.081 --> 14:35.249
Uh, no.

14:36.584 --> 14:38.043
It's just that…

14:38.127 --> 14:40.671
I hadn't considered it, really, until now.

14:40.754 --> 14:43.048
Not getting married after dating.

14:44.466 --> 14:45.718
I want to say

14:45.801 --> 14:48.220
I don't want you to misunderstand
what I think of you.

14:48.846 --> 14:51.807
Not wanting to get married doesn't mean
I'm any less serious about us.

14:51.891 --> 14:54.184
- I'm not trying to lead you on.
- I know.

14:58.564 --> 14:59.607
I'm thinking about…

15:01.442 --> 15:04.904
what would we do when we're that serious?

15:07.531 --> 15:09.450
If you don't wind up getting married,

15:10.409 --> 15:14.330
how do you know when you've reached
the height of your love?

15:18.375 --> 15:21.170
[Si-woo] Sleep is heavily affected
by temperature.

15:22.046 --> 15:23.088
When the weather is warm,

15:23.881 --> 15:26.133
our central nervous systems
are stimulated,

15:26.759 --> 15:28.552
and we have trouble falling asleep.

15:30.888 --> 15:32.890
[calm music playing]

15:41.315 --> 15:42.399
[groans]

15:43.317 --> 15:46.236
[Si-woo] A blizzard of thoughts
swirls in my head these nights.

15:48.113 --> 15:49.615
When I have too many thoughts at once,

15:50.115 --> 15:52.201
my heart gets confused.

15:52.284 --> 15:55.329
And a confused heart can only bring more

15:56.413 --> 15:59.333
and more and more thoughts.

16:02.795 --> 16:03.921
Too hot.

16:04.004 --> 16:06.548
Ugh. It's so hot.

16:07.424 --> 16:12.805
EPISODE 10
TROPICAL NIGHT

16:13.389 --> 16:17.309
The temperature last night
hit a low at just over 25 in Seoul.

16:17.393 --> 16:20.479
We had our first tropical night
of the season and of the year.

16:20.562 --> 16:22.648
- [door opens]
- It's really hot this morning as well…

16:22.731 --> 16:23.774
- Good morning.
- The temperatures will rise

16:23.857 --> 16:26.986
to exceed 31 degrees
during the day in many areas.

16:27.069 --> 16:30.280
- Ugh. Today's gonna be a rough one.
- I know. This is why

16:30.364 --> 16:33.450
I was hoping for rain,
cool the heat down a little.

16:33.534 --> 16:35.035
[TV chatter]

16:35.119 --> 16:36.996
Humidity is high, too.

16:37.079 --> 16:38.747
So, of course, we've got heat.

16:41.333 --> 16:44.294
Why are you worried? Your face.

16:44.378 --> 16:45.921
Did you sleep all right?

16:46.005 --> 16:47.423
Oh, I just got too hot.

16:50.843 --> 16:52.511
We're probably making it worse.

16:52.594 --> 16:54.847
'Cause you have to have your door closed.

16:54.930 --> 16:56.890
Thankfully, I don't like
to keep the door open

16:56.974 --> 16:58.726
even when I'm alone and it's hot.

16:58.809 --> 17:00.185
So don't worry.

17:01.937 --> 17:03.063
I'm sorry, still.

17:03.731 --> 17:06.650
I'll go back home whenever I can.

17:06.734 --> 17:08.485
Well, no pressure for now.

17:08.569 --> 17:10.779
[both chuckle]

17:13.657 --> 17:14.616
[sighs]

17:15.284 --> 17:17.786
[Dong-han] Oh. Look at him.

17:17.870 --> 17:19.747
You didn't sleep, either, did you?

17:20.330 --> 17:21.165
Why?

17:21.749 --> 17:24.043
It'll stay warm for a while now.

17:24.126 --> 17:26.211
It won't be fun.
[groans]

17:26.920 --> 17:28.964
Hey, can I shower first?

17:29.048 --> 17:30.090
Okay.

17:33.677 --> 17:34.803
[door closes]

17:39.725 --> 17:41.185
You didn't sleep well?

17:41.268 --> 17:42.728
It was too hot.

17:45.272 --> 17:46.273
Yeah. It was.

17:51.487 --> 17:53.489
Um…
[grunts]

17:54.990 --> 17:57.993
Everyone, you've all been
waiting for this for so long.

17:58.077 --> 18:01.121
What I have here
is the big three must-haves for newlyweds.

18:01.205 --> 18:03.123
[host] Warm weather is here,
so we have an air conditioner,

18:03.207 --> 18:04.833
a refrigerator, and a washing machine--

18:04.917 --> 18:06.251
- Let's turn on the news.
- Yeah.

18:06.335 --> 18:10.089
…analyzing last year's total death
and birth rate, compared to marriage rate,

18:10.172 --> 18:11.924
- we can plainly see that the date--
- [beeps]

18:12.007 --> 18:14.134
- Coffee sounds good, no?
- Oh, and I can make some toast.

18:14.218 --> 18:15.344
- Sure.
- Okay.

18:20.099 --> 18:21.683
[elevator operator] Doors opening.

18:29.566 --> 18:32.528
Stranger things have happened, you know?

18:32.611 --> 18:36.573
Romance is completely unpredictable,
you'll never know what will happen.

18:36.657 --> 18:39.201
Especially if they're working together
every day.

18:39.284 --> 18:40.410
Hey.

18:40.494 --> 18:42.538
You never know.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.166
- Oh, hey, did you have breakfast?
- [Seok-ho] Mm.

18:51.713 --> 18:53.757
[elevator operator] Doors closing.

18:56.343 --> 18:59.721
[sighs]
Are you really making kimchi today?

18:59.805 --> 19:02.516
Hey, Ma, do you really need all that?

19:02.599 --> 19:05.352
Making moist young radish kimchi
with cold noodles is nutritious

19:05.435 --> 19:06.979
- and it's delicious.
- Yeah, I know that.

19:07.062 --> 19:09.481
But all this is gonna make
an insane amount.

19:09.565 --> 19:11.233
I might have a plan.

19:11.316 --> 19:13.610
- Here. Thank you.
- Thanks. Have a good day.

19:13.694 --> 19:14.903
Come on, there isn't much time.

19:14.987 --> 19:17.906
I've gotta get cooking. This kimchi needs
to be ready by the end of today.

19:19.533 --> 19:22.619
A plan? What are you doing?
When you say you have a plan,

19:22.703 --> 19:25.455
I start to get scared,
you'll make Ha-kyung mad.

19:27.374 --> 19:28.709
The…

19:29.877 --> 19:33.130
handsome guy, he lives above her.
My plan is to get him.

19:33.213 --> 19:35.799
- Huh?
- That guy.

19:35.883 --> 19:39.678
The guy. The guy who kept the food
for so long that you gave Ha-kyung.

19:39.761 --> 19:40.888
Oh, in 1302?

19:40.971 --> 19:44.308
Guess what? Ha-kyung said
he's on her team at work.

19:44.391 --> 19:45.225
Really?

19:46.018 --> 19:47.686
Why didn't he say that
when I talked to him?

19:47.769 --> 19:48.854
Huh?

19:49.438 --> 19:51.565
- You have talked?
- I… I don't know.

19:51.648 --> 19:54.151
We ran into each other once or twice.

19:54.651 --> 19:56.528
I think he might be a nice guy.

19:57.112 --> 20:00.073
No, no, no. You're setting her up
with another stranger.

20:00.157 --> 20:03.911
Exactly, yes, and you can help
if you talk again.

20:04.536 --> 20:06.997
- What?
- Don't play dumb.

20:07.080 --> 20:10.209
You have to do reconnaissance
to see if he's actually good enough.

20:10.292 --> 20:12.669
And if he is, then I'll make a suggestion.

20:13.295 --> 20:15.839
- Huh?
- Wow.

20:19.384 --> 20:21.929
I have a question
about the aerological data from Seoul…

20:24.806 --> 20:28.101
CHIEF TEAM TWO, DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

20:28.185 --> 20:30.229
[playful music playing]

20:33.941 --> 20:35.859
- [tapping on table]
- Mrs. Oh.

20:36.902 --> 20:40.447
- Come on. Mrs. Oh!
- Huh? What?

20:41.740 --> 20:43.992
Here. Look at the AWS numbers in Taebaek.

20:44.076 --> 20:45.619
Does that look right?

20:45.702 --> 20:47.579
Yes, why?

20:47.663 --> 20:51.333
[yawns]

20:51.416 --> 20:52.834
You seem tired. Are you okay?

20:52.918 --> 20:55.254
Oh, way too hot to sleep.

20:55.337 --> 20:58.048
Oh, our youngest couldn't sleep all night,

20:58.131 --> 21:00.801
so I had to stay up, too.

21:00.884 --> 21:02.636
I guess it's showing.

21:02.719 --> 21:04.721
We can't have the AC on, either.

21:05.889 --> 21:07.015
Couldn't your husband help?

21:07.099 --> 21:09.643
[scoffs]
He has to focus on studying.

21:10.310 --> 21:12.187
[yawns]
Since we're committed for a year,

21:12.271 --> 21:15.023
I said to go all-in,
so he'll have no regrets.

21:15.107 --> 21:15.983
[yawns]

21:16.066 --> 21:17.693
Well, it's so bad.

21:17.776 --> 21:19.903
I'm gonna splash some water on my face.

21:21.154 --> 21:22.239
Oh!

21:24.533 --> 21:25.450
[sighs]

21:26.034 --> 21:28.662
It'd be faster for her to take the exam,
she'd get promoted.

21:30.789 --> 21:34.501
She out-scored all the other Level Sevens
when she first came to KMA, you know?

21:34.584 --> 21:36.753
Perfectionist and focused,
she's lightning-fast,

21:36.837 --> 21:37.879
and has good leadership, too.

21:38.547 --> 21:41.508
So everyone thought
she'd be the next director.

21:42.009 --> 21:44.177
But she got married, had kids, and then…

21:44.261 --> 21:45.637
She couldn't do it all, anymore.

21:45.721 --> 21:48.140
I think that's why she's been stuck
for so long.

21:48.223 --> 21:51.685
And she has to take care
of her husband now with everything else.

21:51.768 --> 21:53.145
It must be hard.

21:53.729 --> 21:56.064
Good for her,
I couldn't last a day in her shoes.

21:56.148 --> 21:57.107
Could you?

21:57.691 --> 22:00.027
You can when it's for your kids.

22:00.110 --> 22:02.404
Mm. You're right.

22:04.031 --> 22:06.408
Did you… Did you not sleep too, director?

22:07.034 --> 22:09.077
Oh, the heat got to me.

22:09.161 --> 22:11.455
- Good talk.
- Huh.

22:13.206 --> 22:15.917
We should be exempt from weather
since we work here.

22:20.589 --> 22:24.301
- [Ju-yeong] Hey, Chae Yu-jin.
- Huh? Is that…

22:24.843 --> 22:26.470
They let a city gangster in here?

22:26.553 --> 22:30.265
I guess that's what happens
when there's no drama in the city.

22:30.348 --> 22:31.308
[scoffs]

22:31.391 --> 22:33.018
So you thought you could find
a story here?

22:33.101 --> 22:34.811
You know what they say.

22:34.895 --> 22:37.439
"The KMA will save you
when there's nothing going on."

22:37.522 --> 22:39.983
If I hang around here,
something will turn up, you know?

22:41.109 --> 22:42.486
Also, uh…

22:42.569 --> 22:43.945
Is the food any good in this place?

22:44.696 --> 22:45.572
It's good.

22:45.655 --> 22:47.199
Okay. See you around.

22:49.159 --> 22:53.163
[cell phone buzzing]

22:56.249 --> 22:57.084
What's going on?

22:57.167 --> 22:59.169
[senior reporter]
I heard Heo Ju-yeong is at the KMA.

23:03.215 --> 23:05.967
- What? How did you hear?
- Ugh. No need to know that.

23:06.051 --> 23:09.179
Don't think about coming back
if that bastard steals your story.

23:09.721 --> 23:11.890
There's nothing to steal.
I don't have a story.

23:11.973 --> 23:14.768
Miss Chae, if you don't fully understand,
that's how that leech works.

23:14.851 --> 23:17.187
Once he's set foot in the KMA,

23:17.270 --> 23:19.481
he'll invent something that's newsworthy.

23:19.564 --> 23:20.690
So watch out.

23:21.399 --> 23:23.318
It's your territory at the end of the day.

23:23.401 --> 23:26.530
So if he steals a story from under you,
you know what happens, right?

23:26.613 --> 23:27.447
Yeah.

23:27.531 --> 23:29.241
Think about how he'll attack
your co-workers.

23:29.324 --> 23:31.952
- Now, do what you have to do.
- Okay, okay, I got it.

23:33.328 --> 23:34.204
[beeps]

23:35.872 --> 23:38.375
Oh. Hello, I'm from Munmin Daily.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.918
[Ju-yeong] Wow. You're busy.

23:40.460 --> 23:41.294
[sighs]

23:42.087 --> 23:45.507
[Ha-kyung] At the moment, we're unsure
of where the stationary front went.

23:45.590 --> 23:47.759
The North Pacific's anticyclone
is expanding,

23:47.843 --> 23:51.304
so all the hot humid air
is occupying the Korean peninsula.

23:51.388 --> 23:53.473
As long as it does,
the heat will continue,

23:53.557 --> 23:57.644
and the warm nights, meaning
over 25 degrees, will stay as well.

23:59.563 --> 24:01.648
Oh, boy. And if the warm nights
stick around,

24:01.731 --> 24:03.108
electricity use will go up.

24:03.191 --> 24:05.944
And then we'll have
to prepare for blackouts.

24:06.820 --> 24:09.030
Also, we know that the press
will influence the public.

24:09.114 --> 24:11.158
They'll make everyone panic saying,

24:11.241 --> 24:12.909
"It's a sauna."

24:12.993 --> 24:14.953
Or "The deadliest heat wave
of the century."

24:15.036 --> 24:16.705
I'd say that makes a bigger issue.

24:16.788 --> 24:18.039
[sighs]

24:19.833 --> 24:22.419
We've thought that might be a problem,
so we distributed

24:22.502 --> 24:23.920
some official guidelines already.

24:24.004 --> 24:26.756
And the Office of the Spokesperson
will do what we can to limit it.

24:28.800 --> 24:29.676
[Bong-chan] Okay.

24:30.719 --> 24:31.553
Hm?

24:34.723 --> 24:36.558
[indistinct chatter]

24:38.310 --> 24:40.395
Sir, is there a problem?

24:40.478 --> 24:41.438
Oh, no.

24:51.740 --> 24:53.658
[Ha-kyung] That brings us to the end
of today's meeting.

24:53.742 --> 24:55.243
Okay. Great job, everyone.

24:55.327 --> 24:57.704
- Thank you all.
- Thank you.

25:01.333 --> 25:04.961
[background chatter]

25:07.339 --> 25:08.798
Hey, come with me.

25:18.058 --> 25:19.184
What's this?

25:20.268 --> 25:21.478
Should we sit?

25:43.333 --> 25:45.418
If you told me we'd be
having this conversation,

25:45.502 --> 25:47.045
I wouldn't believe you.

25:47.128 --> 25:49.631
I wanna know what it's like to be married.

25:53.593 --> 25:54.594
What?

25:54.678 --> 25:57.180
- You're asking me? Seriously?
- Yes, I am.

25:57.764 --> 25:59.599
It's just 'cause I genuinely want to know.

26:00.642 --> 26:01.685
Why?

26:02.310 --> 26:03.728
Lee Si-woo asked you?

26:05.105 --> 26:06.356
I shouldn't have asked.

26:06.439 --> 26:08.733
Ah, okay, okay.
I'll give you a real answer.

26:10.735 --> 26:13.571
[sighs]
What is it like, really?

26:14.572 --> 26:19.327
It's hard to define it as just… as either…

26:19.911 --> 26:21.579
worth it or not. You know what I'm saying?

26:22.998 --> 26:24.165
I know.

26:25.041 --> 26:29.754
Well, it's… you go in thinking that all
you need is for each person to be happy,

26:29.838 --> 26:31.631
but it's more complicated,
that's not true.

26:31.715 --> 26:35.927
There are million other things
that come into play.

26:36.011 --> 26:38.722
And you think there'll be twice
as much drama for the two of us.

26:38.805 --> 26:41.182
Though for us, it's ten times more.

26:42.684 --> 26:45.353
And you already know that.

26:45.437 --> 26:47.981
At the very beginning,
things were rough for us.

26:48.732 --> 26:52.402
We both thought we should be happy now,
but we weren't, for some reason.

26:52.902 --> 26:55.947
I felt like a failure. We started
getting upset over the little things.

26:59.034 --> 27:00.785
Also…

27:02.245 --> 27:05.582
Oh, and before we got married,
we could be selfish.

27:06.333 --> 27:09.419
And now, we're considerate

27:09.502 --> 27:12.922
in ways we never thought
we would've guessed before the wedding.

27:13.673 --> 27:17.052
Things changed. Relationships and things
that used to feel so simple,

27:17.135 --> 27:18.595
became really overwhelming.

27:20.472 --> 27:23.224
And for me, it's been interesting

27:23.308 --> 27:25.852
seeing us change and be vulnerable
like we couldn't before.

27:26.436 --> 27:29.856
Accepting those changes
has been a struggle for the two of us.

27:45.205 --> 27:47.749
Is that the guy? The Munmin leech?

27:47.832 --> 27:48.917
Hm?

27:52.420 --> 27:53.588
[exhales deeply]

27:53.671 --> 27:55.215
Why would they send him here?

27:55.298 --> 27:59.886
You can't be so desperate for a story
that you'd give up on morality.

28:01.221 --> 28:02.055
[sighs]

28:04.891 --> 28:06.226
I'm on it.

28:10.647 --> 28:12.315
Can I speak with you?

28:17.195 --> 28:19.656
[Yu-jin] All right, here we go,
your strawberry smoothie.

28:20.657 --> 28:21.991
You know, I'm busy.

28:22.075 --> 28:22.992
[chuckles]
I do.

28:23.076 --> 28:25.245
But I wanted to get our guest a smoothie.

28:25.328 --> 28:28.289
Well, if you really wanted to dazzle me,
you'd get me a drink.

28:29.833 --> 28:30.667
Mm.

28:32.085 --> 28:34.504
I heard you got married.
You got that glow.

28:34.587 --> 28:35.880
I do?
[chuckles]

28:35.964 --> 28:38.758
And the lucky guy,
he works for the KMA, too?

28:39.426 --> 28:40.593
Mm, yeah.

28:43.805 --> 28:46.057
Oh, so you must know all the secrets here.

28:46.141 --> 28:48.601
I wanna know any rumors going around.

28:48.685 --> 28:53.314
Or maybe there's, hm, a power struggle
going on within the KMA.

28:53.398 --> 28:57.110
Or some kind of discrimination?
Any kind of misconduct.

28:57.193 --> 28:59.821
People wanna know
what their officials do all day.

29:00.989 --> 29:02.991
That's why I want to talk to you.

29:03.074 --> 29:04.117
Go on.

29:04.909 --> 29:09.330
Recently, there's a very
high-level conflict that's on-going.

29:09.414 --> 29:10.874
Okay. Who? Details.

29:10.957 --> 29:12.959
I wanna know everything.

29:13.543 --> 29:15.295
High-level, we've got…

29:16.171 --> 29:17.922
General Director Bong-chan…

29:18.006 --> 29:19.674
No, higher.

29:19.758 --> 29:21.134
Way higher,

29:22.177 --> 29:24.679
mT and mP.

29:25.764 --> 29:29.017
mT, mP?

29:34.898 --> 29:35.857
Boo!

29:35.940 --> 29:37.066
- [gasps]
- You're scared?

29:37.150 --> 29:38.401
[shushes]

29:38.485 --> 29:39.569
[Ki-jun] Oh, it's Yu-jin.

29:40.069 --> 29:41.571
- Isn't that…
- Huh?

29:41.654 --> 29:43.072
Mr. Heo Ju-yeong from Munmin Daily?

29:43.740 --> 29:45.033
Who's that?

29:45.116 --> 29:47.494
The Butcher 'cause his articles
cut people down.

29:48.620 --> 29:51.122
[Min-jun] You know wherever he shows up,

29:51.206 --> 29:53.583
someone's probably gonna lose
their job from his story.

29:53.666 --> 29:56.002
I just don't know
why he'd come to the KMA.

29:56.085 --> 29:58.213
Why is she acting like his best friend?

30:09.641 --> 30:12.310
…mT? m…

30:12.393 --> 30:13.394
Who are they?

30:14.395 --> 30:16.523
They're code names, huh? Tell me.

30:18.775 --> 30:22.904
mT is the Pacific Northern air mass.

30:22.987 --> 30:24.948
mP is the Okhotsk Sea air mass.

30:26.199 --> 30:30.036
The only power struggle that matters here
is the air masses this season.

30:32.288 --> 30:35.875
If you didn't know that, I'm not sure
you're qualified to write about us.

30:40.004 --> 30:41.798
I guess you could still hang out, though?

30:41.881 --> 30:44.717
[chuckles]
Um…

30:45.510 --> 30:46.719
So you're saying…

30:47.262 --> 30:51.057
I'm on your territory
and I should piss off?

30:51.641 --> 30:53.101
I'm saying that

30:53.184 --> 30:55.937
if a wonderful reporter like you
covers the smaller stories as well,

30:56.020 --> 30:58.523
new reporters will have a harder time.

30:58.606 --> 31:00.108
It's just the truth, you do it, too.

31:01.317 --> 31:03.319
Uh, if I refuse?

31:03.403 --> 31:07.156
I'd report on a writer whose ethics
are below journalistic standards.

31:07.824 --> 31:10.493
I'd rather be harassed
for shaking the order of things

31:11.077 --> 31:14.539
than stand here and watch you
invent what should be my story.

31:14.622 --> 31:16.165
Somebody is growing up.

31:16.833 --> 31:18.877
Coming from you, that's a compliment.
Thank you.

31:22.797 --> 31:24.799
[playful music playing]

31:29.762 --> 31:30.889
[chuckles]

31:34.017 --> 31:36.603
[sighs]
Some piece of crap.

31:37.270 --> 31:38.897
- They'll let anyone be a reporter--
- Oh!

31:38.980 --> 31:39.981
Uh…

31:41.274 --> 31:42.525
Are you okay?

31:43.318 --> 31:44.360
I'm okay.

31:48.114 --> 31:48.990
Yu-jin.

31:51.075 --> 31:52.869
Can I talk to you for a second?

31:58.291 --> 32:00.168
[Si-woo] Time really does fly.

32:00.251 --> 32:02.837
Yesterday, I swear I needed
my winter jacket.

32:03.504 --> 32:04.672
It does.

32:05.673 --> 32:09.052
It's been a million years
since my wedding day.

32:13.056 --> 32:14.223
What can I do for you?

32:18.770 --> 32:19.771
Um…

32:21.230 --> 32:22.899
When I told you

32:23.858 --> 32:26.361
that I never wanted to marry anybody,

32:27.111 --> 32:28.655
what did you think?

32:33.910 --> 32:35.495
Hmm…

32:37.497 --> 32:38.790
In one word, I was…

32:40.041 --> 32:41.000
dumbfounded.

32:42.752 --> 32:44.045
"What's his problem?"

32:44.128 --> 32:45.964
"Why didn't he tell me sooner?"

32:47.215 --> 32:49.842
At first, I was freaking out, absolutely.

32:51.386 --> 32:52.387
And then?

32:54.722 --> 32:56.599
I thought I could change your mind,

32:56.683 --> 32:59.477
then I realized I shouldn't have
to convince you.

32:59.560 --> 33:01.437
And I realized we just…

33:01.521 --> 33:04.148
we wanted totally different things,
that's all.

33:06.275 --> 33:10.196
So I knew there was no way
we could have it work.

33:15.576 --> 33:18.579
[breathes deeply]

33:19.497 --> 33:21.666
After I figured out that

33:23.626 --> 33:26.295
we would have to call it off one day,

33:28.047 --> 33:30.425
I fell out of love with you,
though it took a while.

33:33.678 --> 33:35.638
Then suddenly, I met Ki-jun.

33:42.103 --> 33:44.022
[breathes deeply]

34:02.123 --> 34:03.624
[Yu-jin] After I figured out that

34:04.208 --> 34:06.836
we would have to call it off one day,

34:08.212 --> 34:10.715
I fell out of love with you,
though it took a while.

34:22.727 --> 34:23.895
[sighs]

34:23.978 --> 34:26.189
Huh? Huh?

34:26.272 --> 34:28.149
What's with the temperature in Yeouido?

34:28.232 --> 34:30.234
[tense music playing]

34:31.319 --> 34:33.529
Uh, is there a problem with it?

34:33.613 --> 34:36.032
The website says it's 36.7 degrees.

34:36.115 --> 34:39.160
That means it's somewhat 7 degrees
hotter than any of the areas next to it.

34:39.243 --> 34:40.953
Is it? Is it? Did anyone do the MQC?

34:42.163 --> 34:43.831
Oh, I did sign off earlier.

34:45.291 --> 34:47.168
Did you look at it? This is wrong.

34:47.794 --> 34:49.253
Uh, hang on. Give me a sec.

34:49.962 --> 34:52.590
Take it down, now. Put a blank
on the weather portal if you have to.

34:52.673 --> 34:55.927
- We can't cause more confusion.
- Yeah, I'm doing that.

34:56.010 --> 34:58.596
- Oh, no, that's…
- Here, let me help.

35:16.114 --> 35:18.074
Huh? There's no way.

35:18.157 --> 35:20.368
[indistinct chatter]

35:26.165 --> 35:27.708
Hm? Is there a mistake?

35:28.960 --> 35:31.796
Yeouido's high. The temperature is wrong.

35:32.296 --> 35:33.714
Just a typo, I guess.

35:34.298 --> 35:35.341
Typo?

35:39.512 --> 35:40.555
Show me.

35:50.022 --> 35:51.023
Hey.

35:53.401 --> 35:54.360
Uh…

35:55.027 --> 35:56.988
Is Mrs. Oh gonna be okay?

35:57.488 --> 36:00.867
An error on MQC
is a pretty serious sign of negligence.

36:00.950 --> 36:03.661
They'll reprimand her according to policy.

36:03.744 --> 36:06.539
But they know everyone messes up.

36:10.918 --> 36:14.088
- The things you say amaze me sometimes.
- Huh?

36:14.172 --> 36:15.840
We're public officials.

36:15.923 --> 36:17.884
We're not allowed to mess up.

36:22.096 --> 36:23.681
[sighs]

36:26.767 --> 36:28.060
Where are you going?

36:29.145 --> 36:30.438
I need air.

36:35.026 --> 36:36.194
[Soo-jin] What happens now?

36:36.277 --> 36:38.779
You have to do a write-up
for Mr. Bong-chan?

36:38.863 --> 36:40.573
How long was the error live on the portal?

36:40.656 --> 36:42.074
Less than five minutes, I'd say.

36:44.785 --> 36:47.830
Well, I'll figure it out.
You get back to work, okay?

36:47.914 --> 36:48.873
Okay.

37:05.014 --> 37:06.098
Oh, thanks.

37:10.770 --> 37:13.397
I'm not usually this spacey.

37:13.481 --> 37:14.482
I know.

37:14.565 --> 37:16.150
A mistake like this is unprecedented.

37:16.234 --> 37:17.401
I'm sorry.

37:18.236 --> 37:21.030
I haven't had a good night's sleep
in a couple of days or so.

37:21.614 --> 37:24.700
I don't know, I shouldn't make excuses.
It's unforgivable.

37:26.244 --> 37:27.286
I'm so sorry.

37:29.538 --> 37:32.500
I think you should take an hour
and rest in the night-duty room.

37:33.376 --> 37:36.254
- But the error report--
- I can handle it without you.

37:37.505 --> 37:38.547
Thanks for that.

37:43.427 --> 37:45.638
Um, director?

37:47.306 --> 37:50.101
Think before you marry anybody.

37:52.520 --> 37:55.481
I know you might not wanna hear it,
maybe it's not my place to say.

37:56.274 --> 37:58.776
But when I heard
you called off the wedding,

37:59.360 --> 38:01.070
I felt really proud of you.

38:03.406 --> 38:05.616
I was almost jealous, honestly.

38:05.700 --> 38:08.703
Because once you're married
and you have kids,

38:08.786 --> 38:11.247
'cause that's what you do,
not 'cause you really wanted…

38:12.873 --> 38:15.084
[sighs]
And then there's no way out.

38:17.753 --> 38:20.965
You're a free woman.
You deserve to get anything you want.

38:22.550 --> 38:24.385
Right now, you can do anything
you want to.

38:25.678 --> 38:28.347
Even if it's just enjoying time
to yourself.

38:34.645 --> 38:37.606
[indistinct chatter]

38:37.690 --> 38:40.192
[guide] If you're ready,
let's go in, follow me.

38:40.276 --> 38:41.485
[all] Okay.

38:46.282 --> 38:47.992
[line rings]

38:48.075 --> 38:49.076
[Hyang-rae] Hello?

38:49.160 --> 38:51.370
Hey, is Bo-mi at school today?

38:54.707 --> 38:56.459
She has a field trip today.

38:57.126 --> 38:58.461
Why? Is she okay?

38:58.544 --> 38:59.920
I just saw her. Bo-mi.

39:00.504 --> 39:02.340
- You what?
- She's at the KMA.

39:02.423 --> 39:04.050
Okay, talk later.

39:04.133 --> 39:05.217
[beeps]

39:08.846 --> 39:10.139
What was that?

39:19.482 --> 39:21.984
You should have called me
and said you'd be here.

39:22.068 --> 39:23.402
I could pull some strings,

39:23.486 --> 39:26.030
so you and your friends
can see the cool stuff behind the scenes.

39:26.113 --> 39:27.573
You're a public official.

39:28.240 --> 39:30.326
You wouldn't abuse public resources,
would you?

39:31.994 --> 39:34.955
Of course not. You're right.
[chuckles]

39:35.039 --> 39:37.124
So, now, what have you seen?
Where did you go?

39:37.208 --> 39:38.959
The room for Forecasting and Earthquakes.

39:39.043 --> 39:40.127
Oh.

39:40.711 --> 39:41.879
What do you think of it all?

39:41.962 --> 39:45.174
You can see how hard
we work every day, right?

39:46.717 --> 39:48.052
I've already seen that.

39:48.135 --> 39:49.095
Huh?

39:49.178 --> 39:50.679
Mom always says

39:51.972 --> 39:53.641
that only smart people really know

39:53.724 --> 39:55.267
how hard forecasters work.

39:56.644 --> 39:57.853
I guess.

39:57.937 --> 40:00.815
That's right. So you're smart,
'cause you knew.

40:00.898 --> 40:02.108
That's how it works, right?

40:03.943 --> 40:06.487
[chuckling]

40:06.570 --> 40:08.489
Are you coming back another day?

40:08.572 --> 40:11.242
One more day, next week. Why?

40:12.493 --> 40:15.246
I think you need to try
the food in the cafeteria. It's good.

40:15.329 --> 40:16.664
We'll have lunch together.

40:16.747 --> 40:18.165
Just call me when you're here.

40:18.249 --> 40:21.252
Unless that would be abuse
of public resources.

40:22.628 --> 40:24.880
Well, I'll think about it.

40:25.798 --> 40:26.757
Okay.

40:27.425 --> 40:30.511
Think about it. You would have fun.

40:30.594 --> 40:33.013
[both chuckle]

40:36.267 --> 40:38.102
Why did you want to go there, anyway?

40:38.185 --> 40:40.271
I told you. I went for school.

40:40.354 --> 40:42.356
There were other trips. Why the KMA?

40:42.440 --> 40:45.192
My teacher told me
to get into the high school I like,

40:45.276 --> 40:48.779
I need more science-focused activities,
so I thought I'd go.

40:48.863 --> 40:50.906
You could have at least told me about it.

40:50.990 --> 40:53.075
If I did, you would've said I couldn't go.

40:53.159 --> 40:53.993
What?

40:54.076 --> 40:55.619
You always say the same thing.

40:55.703 --> 40:58.956
You won't even call when it's important,
'cause we can't disturb his work.

40:59.039 --> 41:00.875
And you're sad doing everything alone.

41:00.958 --> 41:02.668
I wanted to see it myself.

41:03.586 --> 41:04.587
[scoffs]

41:04.670 --> 41:06.422
What exactly did you want to see?

41:06.505 --> 41:08.382
I want to know what Dad does at work.

41:08.466 --> 41:11.135
Is it really so important
that he had to abandon us?

41:11.218 --> 41:13.137
Why can't he find more time?

41:14.263 --> 41:15.764
Don't I deserve to know that?

41:18.934 --> 41:20.769
So what did you learn
while you were there?

41:20.853 --> 41:23.522
- It was the first day. I don't know.
- So you're going another day?

41:23.606 --> 41:25.065
Sometime next week.

41:36.452 --> 41:38.787
[chuckling]

41:38.871 --> 41:40.498
You're sure in a good mood today.

41:41.540 --> 41:42.583
Well…

41:42.666 --> 41:46.837
My daughter visited,
there was a field trip to the KMA.

41:49.548 --> 41:51.759
I realized something interesting.

41:52.468 --> 41:53.719
She actually…

41:54.637 --> 41:56.263
looks like me, a little.

41:56.347 --> 41:58.098
[both chuckle]

41:58.182 --> 42:00.643
That's not interesting.
It's normal, you know?

42:00.726 --> 42:03.062
- I guess it is, huh?
- [both chuckle]

42:03.145 --> 42:06.732
I can't get over how weird it is
having a kid.

42:07.608 --> 42:09.610
I feel like I don't understand her at all.

42:10.194 --> 42:12.321
Somehow. I don't know why.

42:12.404 --> 42:14.740
She still makes me laugh like no one else.

42:15.866 --> 42:17.743
- Oh.
- You're walking on clouds.

42:18.661 --> 42:20.829
Wait until you get married
and have a family.

42:20.913 --> 42:22.998
I can't find the right words
to explain it.

42:23.082 --> 42:25.876
You think you know? You can't.
Not until you're doing it.

42:25.960 --> 42:28.337
Okay, coming from the guy that left home.

42:28.921 --> 42:30.631
You still feel that,
even though it hurt you?

42:30.714 --> 42:33.092
Of course, family is everything.

42:34.593 --> 42:37.846
Si-woo, you shouldn't set aside family
for some adventure.

42:37.930 --> 42:38.764
Like what I did.

42:38.847 --> 42:41.141
[inhales sharply]
Do everything you can to stick together.

42:41.225 --> 42:43.477
You'll always regret
staying away too long.

42:44.645 --> 42:46.689
- It's just not worth it.
- [cell phone buzzes]

42:46.772 --> 42:48.732
'Cause… Hold on. Oh.

42:50.317 --> 42:52.278
[Hyang-rae] Stop by
when you're done with work.

42:52.361 --> 42:53.487
Oh, speaking of.

42:53.571 --> 42:54.947
My wife.

42:55.739 --> 42:57.741
- Oh, uh… Yeah.
- Okay.

42:57.825 --> 42:59.368
- Go without me.
- Okay.

42:59.451 --> 43:02.371
- I should go… Go home.
- Yeah, good luck.

43:02.454 --> 43:04.290
- Thanks. Okay.
- Okay.

43:05.165 --> 43:06.667
- Have a good night.
- Okay.

43:12.298 --> 43:13.132
Hello, how are you?

43:13.215 --> 43:15.426
Uh, what do you want?

43:15.509 --> 43:16.594
[chuckles]

43:16.677 --> 43:19.096
- This is for you. Here.
- Oh, what is this?

43:19.179 --> 43:20.347
Kimchi.

43:20.931 --> 43:24.852
My mom made it as a way to say thank you
for holding the sides a while ago.

43:24.935 --> 43:26.228
Oh, that's not necessary.

43:26.312 --> 43:29.023
[chuckles]
Sorry, is there any way

43:29.106 --> 43:31.775
I could come in
and wash my hands real quick?

43:31.859 --> 43:33.819
Oh, it must have leaked
when I carried it up.

43:33.902 --> 43:34.737
[sniffs]

43:34.820 --> 43:36.947
Oh. My hands smell like kimchi, I think.

43:37.031 --> 43:38.157
- Do they?
- I'm sure they're…

43:38.240 --> 43:39.783
- Thanks.
- Wait a minute.

43:40.451 --> 43:42.661
Hang on. Wait a sec.

43:42.745 --> 43:43.704
Ah!

43:53.172 --> 43:54.381
[elevator operator] Doors opening.

44:01.013 --> 44:03.307
Oh, what are you doing there, ma'am?

44:03.390 --> 44:04.892
Huh? Oh…

44:05.392 --> 44:07.144
Uh, I was, uh…

44:09.146 --> 44:10.105
You wanna go in?

44:10.189 --> 44:13.651
Oh, I'm okay. Oh, hey, here.

44:14.777 --> 44:18.197
You should take these to the apartment.

44:19.073 --> 44:21.867
You came all the way here with food.
Please, I insist.

44:21.950 --> 44:23.202
I could…

44:25.412 --> 44:26.872
I'll go for a second.

44:26.955 --> 44:28.415
Good.

44:29.583 --> 44:32.211
[lock beeping]

44:42.388 --> 44:44.264
What are you doing here, Mom?

44:45.099 --> 44:46.892
There are no rules
I can't visit my daughter.

44:46.975 --> 44:48.477
Maybe check your fridge.

44:48.560 --> 44:49.812
Is that enough?

44:54.066 --> 44:56.068
You have to let me know
if you're gonna visit.

44:56.151 --> 44:57.653
- You're making my teammates uncomfortable.
- If that's true,

44:57.736 --> 44:59.571
I'm coming every single day now.

44:59.655 --> 45:01.824
They should be uncomfortable
living with you.

45:04.952 --> 45:06.370
I can handle it. Don't worry.

45:06.453 --> 45:08.539
One day, you'll be married
with a stubborn daughter.

45:08.622 --> 45:10.541
You'll understand why I'm worried then.

45:11.333 --> 45:13.752
Till then, don't get too comfortable.

45:13.836 --> 45:16.380
Senior Um will be back soon.
You should leave before then.

45:16.463 --> 45:18.632
I wouldn't dream of staying here
another second,

45:18.715 --> 45:21.510
- even if you beg me on your knees.
- Oh, here.

45:21.593 --> 45:23.470
I got this for you.

45:24.221 --> 45:25.264
Huh?

45:25.347 --> 45:27.349
- Well, thank you, young man.
- Sure.

45:28.100 --> 45:30.602
Oh, why is she taking so long up there?

45:32.271 --> 45:33.397
She? Who?

45:33.480 --> 45:35.482
[quirky music playing]

45:37.776 --> 45:38.819
Ah…

45:40.404 --> 45:43.949
No, I said… I said that…

45:50.789 --> 45:51.707
[Seok-ho] Here.

45:51.790 --> 45:54.209
Oh, thank you, sir.
[chuckles]

46:00.716 --> 46:02.176
Oh!

46:02.259 --> 46:03.260
[gasps]

46:03.760 --> 46:06.013
You must read a book every day.

46:06.096 --> 46:09.433
It's… No, they're just copies
of the classics.

46:09.516 --> 46:10.726
And he's smartass.

46:10.809 --> 46:12.060
Huh?

46:12.144 --> 46:14.104
Oh, wonderful collection.

46:14.688 --> 46:15.606
Yeah.

46:18.358 --> 46:22.154
You really didn't need to do
any of this for me.

46:22.738 --> 46:26.325
In my family, we never let
a favor go unreturned.

46:26.408 --> 46:28.869
And everyone could use a side dish or two.

46:28.952 --> 46:30.704
What, you eat only dewdrops?

46:30.787 --> 46:32.331
I prefer to cook my own food.

46:33.457 --> 46:35.083
You're particular, aren't you?

46:35.667 --> 46:37.377
Are you an only child?

46:37.461 --> 46:39.588
- Yeah, that's right.
- Mm-hm? Where are you from?

46:39.671 --> 46:41.215
Suwon. Why are you asking me?

46:41.298 --> 46:43.091
I'm curious. I wanted to know.

46:43.175 --> 46:44.676
You work with my sister, I hear.

46:44.760 --> 46:47.137
Yeah, well, that's true.

46:47.221 --> 46:49.723
Tell your mother I'm so grateful and--

46:49.806 --> 46:52.559
You're in the same team
and live in the same place.

46:52.643 --> 46:56.313
Wow. That seems like a sign of something,
it's like destiny.

46:56.396 --> 47:00.234
A lot of our co-workers live
in the building just around this area.

47:01.068 --> 47:03.445
There are six other people working
for the KMA

47:03.529 --> 47:04.780
living in the building.
There could be more.

47:04.863 --> 47:07.074
Oh, it's so convenient.

47:24.383 --> 47:27.344
CITY CROCODILE
BY JIN TAE-KYUNG

47:27.427 --> 47:29.429
[soft music playing]

47:32.558 --> 47:33.433
[clears throat]

47:34.142 --> 47:35.227
Um…

47:36.144 --> 47:39.064
The research was rather lacking,

47:39.147 --> 47:42.234
that's that,
the story was pretty good, so…

47:46.446 --> 47:47.906
What parts did you like?

47:56.832 --> 47:57.958
What?

47:58.041 --> 48:00.085
Tae-kyung is spying on my co-worker?

48:00.168 --> 48:01.795
Listen. It's not--

48:01.878 --> 48:03.672
- Mom! What's wrong with you?
- Don't scream.

48:04.298 --> 48:05.841
[sighs]
We've been over this.

48:05.924 --> 48:08.594
Shin Seok-ho is my subordinate at work.

48:08.677 --> 48:11.138
It's annoying for me.
But how do you think it makes him feel?

48:11.221 --> 48:12.764
How can I look at him at work?

48:14.141 --> 48:15.809
If you need a project,
something to work on,

48:15.892 --> 48:17.394
go fix up your own life!

48:18.729 --> 48:21.481
You're… You're just being cruel now.

48:21.565 --> 48:23.275
I'm your mom. You can't say that.

48:23.358 --> 48:26.236
You have no idea what it's like to lose
sleep worrying about your daughter.

48:26.945 --> 48:28.363
Everything I do is for you.

48:28.447 --> 48:30.115
And you tell me, what?

48:30.198 --> 48:31.408
"Mom, fix your own life"?

48:32.784 --> 48:34.077
[Si-woo] It's not right.

48:36.830 --> 48:39.583
Hear that? Even your guest
thinks you're wrong.

48:41.043 --> 48:42.419
Oh, no, I…

48:42.502 --> 48:45.631
I meant you, ma'am. Not Miss Jin.

48:46.923 --> 48:47.966
Huh?

48:48.050 --> 48:50.260
It's clear that when parents force things
on their children,

48:50.344 --> 48:51.928
even if they say it will be good,

48:52.012 --> 48:54.389
the children never actually end up happy
or whatever it is.

48:55.724 --> 48:57.809
[Mrs. Bae] Hold on, hold on.
Hang on. You're saying

48:57.893 --> 49:00.395
I should just sit around all day
and watch my own flesh and blood

49:00.479 --> 49:01.521
turn into a spinster?

49:02.147 --> 49:04.191
Waste away, turn down the good men?

49:04.274 --> 49:06.234
Lose the best years of her life for what?

49:06.318 --> 49:10.072
It doesn't really matter if she does,
what matters is if she wants to.

49:10.822 --> 49:14.242
You don't know, you're too young.
You're nearly a child.

49:14.326 --> 49:16.870
- You'll learn one day, marriage--
- It's never happening.

49:18.413 --> 49:19.581
What?

49:23.001 --> 49:25.045
Never am I getting married, Mom.

49:29.675 --> 49:33.053
Oh, no. It's… It's too late.

49:33.136 --> 49:35.555
You need to sleep. We'll talk later.

49:36.139 --> 49:37.140
I mean it.

49:38.475 --> 49:40.519
That's how it is, so you can move on.

49:42.312 --> 49:44.022
[Mrs. Bae] No, come on, Ha-kyung.

49:45.232 --> 49:49.361
There's no reason to make a silly decision
out of stubbornness.

49:49.444 --> 49:52.030
Okay, I'll admit.
Your mom went too far today.

49:52.114 --> 49:54.324
It's my fault. I'm sorry. My bad.

49:55.117 --> 49:56.326
I made up my mind, Mom.

49:57.494 --> 50:00.747
You're gonna have a daughter
that's single forever, that's it.

50:00.831 --> 50:03.667
Starting now, no more talk about marriage,
no blind dates,

50:03.750 --> 50:05.210
no more talk about romance.

50:06.128 --> 50:06.962
Ha-kyung.

50:07.045 --> 50:09.381
I need space tonight.
You can see yourself out.

50:10.716 --> 50:11.633
Ah…

50:13.844 --> 50:14.761
[door slams]

50:18.765 --> 50:19.850
[sighs]

50:28.275 --> 50:31.194
That's why they evolved
to have only four toes at the back.

50:32.112 --> 50:33.113
Oh.

50:34.156 --> 50:36.241
You could be a real animal scientist.

50:36.742 --> 50:38.535
Oh, no, I'm no zoologist.

50:39.119 --> 50:40.829
You know enough to be one.

50:40.912 --> 50:43.373
You know so much about animals.

50:45.459 --> 50:47.127
Well, anyone can do that.

50:47.210 --> 50:49.796
I just like them,
so I read about them a lot.

50:49.880 --> 50:51.798
Oh, that's cool.

50:52.299 --> 50:55.135
Oh. What about penguins?

50:55.218 --> 50:57.179
You don't know about penguins, do you?

50:57.929 --> 50:58.889
Penguins?

50:59.389 --> 51:03.059
[chuckles]
I thought, for my next book, it might be

51:03.143 --> 51:04.853
about this penguin who does things.

51:06.229 --> 51:08.899
So any penguin facts
would be really helpful for me.

51:09.900 --> 51:13.361
Well, I… I'd say my favorite animal
are penguins, so, yeah.

51:13.445 --> 51:15.572
[gasps]
What? Seriously?

51:15.655 --> 51:18.492
[shrieks]
That's amazing!

51:19.117 --> 51:20.744
Could you help me with the pictures, then?

51:20.827 --> 51:22.454
[both chuckle]

51:23.455 --> 51:24.331
Yeah?

51:25.165 --> 51:27.125
I guess I could.

51:28.710 --> 51:30.212
You have to tell her.

51:30.879 --> 51:31.880
What?

51:32.380 --> 51:34.966
I want you to tell her yourself right now.

51:35.050 --> 51:36.885
What do you want me to tell her?

51:36.968 --> 51:40.222
That she can't visit the KMA
for the field trip to see you.

51:40.305 --> 51:41.848
You're too busy, right?

51:43.809 --> 51:46.812
I'll find time for her.
It's really not a problem.

51:47.813 --> 51:50.857
It's not like it was my idea.
The whole thing was set up by the school.

51:51.775 --> 51:54.194
I'm happy to see Bo-mi at my work.

51:55.153 --> 51:56.071
I'm not, though.

51:57.572 --> 52:00.367
I'm not comfortable with the two of you
at the KMA.

52:00.951 --> 52:02.244
With your co-workers.

52:08.792 --> 52:10.210
[sighs]

52:33.441 --> 52:34.901
What are you doing here?

52:35.402 --> 52:37.946
I'll call a taxi for you.
It's too hot to walk.

52:39.322 --> 52:40.448
[sighs]

52:41.700 --> 52:42.909
It didn't use to get

52:43.535 --> 52:46.788
this hot even in the middle of summer,
it didn't.

52:47.831 --> 52:51.334
I think the weather is learning
from how people are these days.

52:51.418 --> 52:53.169
Tough, 'cause they have to be.

52:54.546 --> 52:58.258
I think it's incredible
that everyone goes on in this heat.

52:58.967 --> 53:01.052
You agree, then. Everyone is tough now.

53:01.136 --> 53:03.680
You don't think it's the other way around,
where people react

53:03.763 --> 53:04.806
to the world they're in?

53:06.558 --> 53:07.601
Was I too tough?

53:07.684 --> 53:09.811
No. That's not what I meant.

53:11.479 --> 53:12.647
Stick to the weather, kid.

53:12.731 --> 53:15.108
I wish I could.
That'd be a dream come true for me.

53:16.484 --> 53:18.445
I don't understand these kids.

53:20.030 --> 53:24.159
Ma'am, you don't have to worry
about Director Jin too much.

53:24.242 --> 53:25.660
She was probably just angry.

53:25.744 --> 53:28.288
She can change her mind.
It's too big of a decision

53:28.371 --> 53:31.416
to just make a choice
and stick to it one day.

53:34.961 --> 53:37.756
Ha-kyung doesn't say things
without certainty.

53:39.299 --> 53:42.385
If she said something,
she really means it.

53:45.764 --> 53:48.183
I was too hard on her, wasn't I?

53:50.852 --> 53:51.978
[sighs]

54:15.877 --> 54:16.920
[chuckles]

54:24.511 --> 54:25.762
I got her a taxi.

54:30.058 --> 54:32.560
[romantic music playing]

54:32.644 --> 54:34.479
My mom's a lot, isn't she?

54:34.562 --> 54:36.231
Mm…

54:38.441 --> 54:39.275
Well, she…

54:41.277 --> 54:42.779
cares about everything.

54:44.572 --> 54:46.491
That's every mother and her kid.

54:47.075 --> 54:49.869
If that's true, why did you lie to her?

54:49.953 --> 54:51.162
Lie what?

54:52.455 --> 54:53.665
About getting married.

54:54.791 --> 54:57.961
I've heard that saying
"You won't" really shocks people.

54:58.044 --> 55:00.088
You shouldn't do that as a joke.

55:00.797 --> 55:02.048
I was serious.

55:04.801 --> 55:07.095
Well, serious and that I'm considering it.

55:07.804 --> 55:11.433
Like you said, if people are just waiting
to get married or not, it's suffocating.

55:11.516 --> 55:14.686
I don't want a relationship
where we're bringing each other down.

55:24.154 --> 55:26.614
I'm tired. Let's go to bed.

55:46.259 --> 55:47.302
[sighs]

55:49.012 --> 55:50.138
[exhales sharply]

55:52.265 --> 55:53.391
[exhales heavily]

56:10.575 --> 56:11.701
[groans]

56:17.582 --> 56:18.583
[grunts]

56:23.421 --> 56:24.672
[sighs]

56:35.517 --> 56:38.603
Due to the influence of the hot and humid
North Pacific's anticyclone,

56:38.686 --> 56:41.314
temperatures during the day
will rise up to 32 degrees nationwide.

56:41.397 --> 56:43.608
And we'll continue to have warm nights.

56:43.691 --> 56:47.529
Our concern is that citizens
are going increasingly fatigued,

56:47.612 --> 56:49.405
purposely caused by the evening heat.

56:49.489 --> 56:52.075
We'll start to see an increase
in workplace and driving accidents.

56:52.158 --> 56:53.368
If you turn to the chart…

56:53.451 --> 56:55.954
[paper rustling]

56:57.330 --> 56:58.957
The Head Director wants to see you, sir.

57:00.959 --> 57:01.960
You know why?

57:02.669 --> 57:04.295
We're having a meeting. Why?

57:19.018 --> 57:20.228
Director Jin.

57:20.979 --> 57:23.273
Was there an error posted

57:23.356 --> 57:25.275
on the disaster prevention portal
yesterday?

57:25.358 --> 57:27.360
[tense music playing]

57:30.071 --> 57:31.406
[Ha-kyung] Yes, very briefly.

57:31.906 --> 57:33.950
We corrected the information right away.

57:37.412 --> 57:38.246
[sighs]

57:38.329 --> 57:39.706
[tablet clacks]

57:40.582 --> 57:42.417
When were you gonna tell me that?

57:43.126 --> 57:45.879
You should have submitted a report
to me right away!

57:47.547 --> 57:50.133
We're already called
the "Korean Bullshit Administration."

57:50.216 --> 57:52.010
The "KBA!", "Incompetent!"

57:53.887 --> 57:55.680
[Bong-chan] This seems like evidence!

57:55.763 --> 57:58.016
MUNMIN DAILY
INCORRECT INFORMATION ON PORTAL SITE

58:01.519 --> 58:02.854
Jesus.

58:04.314 --> 58:07.609
- Where is the Head Director?
- [Sung-jin] He's in his office right now.

58:07.692 --> 58:08.735
[Bong-chan] Wonderful.

58:10.069 --> 58:11.112
Good morning, sir.

58:12.071 --> 58:13.239
Yes, of course.

58:14.157 --> 58:15.325
Can I see the tablet?

58:19.662 --> 58:21.748
THE FREQUENT MISREPORTS
WERE PREDICTABLE

58:23.333 --> 58:26.002
Oh, no, damn it. They saw it.

58:35.136 --> 58:36.221
[sighs]

58:39.933 --> 58:42.936
[Soo-jin]
Are all reporters totally insane?

58:43.520 --> 58:45.647
It should be illegal
to write stuff like this!

58:46.231 --> 58:47.607
We're only human.

58:47.690 --> 58:49.859
It's almost always accurate. Just a few…

58:52.737 --> 58:54.405
Just one mistake.

58:54.489 --> 58:56.282
They must be bored if they're nitpicking.

58:59.786 --> 59:00.662
Oh.

59:04.499 --> 59:06.876
Someone's probably gonna lose
their job from his story.

59:06.960 --> 59:09.003
[Min-jun] I just don't know
why he'd come to the KMA.

59:09.087 --> 59:11.089
Why is she acting like his best friend?

59:14.717 --> 59:17.303
[Yu-jin] Hey. I didn't miss it.

59:17.387 --> 59:19.389
I chose not to report,
'cause it's nothing.

59:20.765 --> 59:22.642
[sighs]
I know.

59:23.226 --> 59:25.436
It was a small mistake.
It's not worth the page.

59:25.520 --> 59:27.564
And the forecasters
are taking it really hard.

59:28.147 --> 59:29.691
Yes. Okay.

59:31.693 --> 59:34.737
[sighs]
Thanks for hearing my side.

59:35.446 --> 59:36.406
Okay.

59:37.865 --> 59:39.033
Good bye.

59:43.121 --> 59:43.955
[sighs]

59:49.752 --> 59:51.170
We need to talk.

01:00:03.933 --> 01:00:05.018
How is it up there?

01:00:06.144 --> 01:00:08.479
The error
on the disaster prevention portal,

01:00:08.563 --> 01:00:10.023
you tipped him off, didn't you?

01:00:10.815 --> 01:00:11.899
No, I wouldn't.

01:00:11.983 --> 01:00:13.318
I saw it happen.

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:16.362
I saw you whispering with him
in the cafeteria, with Mr. Heo.

01:00:16.446 --> 01:00:17.655
No, I told you.

01:00:17.739 --> 01:00:19.198
You're trying to deny it?

01:00:20.325 --> 01:00:21.951
You've seen how hard everyone works here.

01:00:22.035 --> 01:00:23.328
You know what we do.

01:00:23.411 --> 01:00:25.204
You just had to help
that guy get a story, huh?

01:00:25.288 --> 01:00:26.331
It's a small error.

01:00:26.414 --> 01:00:28.041
What, you never made a mistake?

01:00:30.752 --> 01:00:32.045
Oppa, you…

01:00:33.087 --> 01:00:35.256
You don't want to listen at all, do you?

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:36.507
Why should I listen?

01:00:37.008 --> 01:00:38.843
You're not saying anything believable.

01:00:42.347 --> 01:00:44.057
You really don't trust your wife?

01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:46.059
What?

01:00:46.142 --> 01:00:48.102
How can you marry someone you can't trust?

01:00:48.186 --> 01:00:49.812
You don't even trust me enough
to hear me out.

01:00:49.896 --> 01:00:51.230
So how did this happen, huh?

01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:54.484
Yu-jin, what are you saying?
I'm just talking about the article.

01:00:54.567 --> 01:00:56.194
I wanna know what you did.

01:00:56.277 --> 01:00:58.946
And I wanna know why you married
someone you won't hear out.

01:01:00.490 --> 01:01:02.367
'Cause this doesn't just happen
when we're at work.

01:01:02.450 --> 01:01:04.285
Your trust issues are massive.

01:01:04.369 --> 01:01:07.288
Oppa, how can you think
your wife is so awful?

01:01:09.082 --> 01:01:10.208
I wanna know.

01:01:15.797 --> 01:01:16.964
[Bong-chan] Director Jin.

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:19.926
Can you manage your team,
or is it too intense?

01:01:20.927 --> 01:01:21.928
I'm sorry, sir.

01:01:22.011 --> 01:01:25.181
'Cause this isn't the first time.
How do we fix things?

01:01:25.264 --> 01:01:27.433
Every day, there's something,
even if it's small.

01:01:28.434 --> 01:01:31.771
Will you be able to make it
through the season?

01:01:31.854 --> 01:01:33.773
With things how they are now.

01:01:35.733 --> 01:01:37.360
I need to know if you can't.

01:01:37.443 --> 01:01:39.987
'Cause I need to do some hiring
if it's too much for you.

01:01:40.071 --> 01:01:41.823
I can do it. I've got it, sir.

01:01:41.906 --> 01:01:45.618
The typhoons haven't even started yet,
and when they do, teamwork's important.

01:01:47.245 --> 01:01:48.579
Don't forget that.

01:01:49.497 --> 01:01:51.290
Yes, sir. I won't.

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:52.667
Go on.

01:01:53.376 --> 01:01:55.211
Oh, and who are you sending to Jeju?

01:01:55.837 --> 01:01:56.796
What?

01:01:56.879 --> 01:01:59.799
We'll have a typhoon soon.
We need a direct report.

01:01:59.882 --> 01:02:01.843
You need to send someone from your team.

01:02:01.926 --> 01:02:04.887
- You haven't picked?
- Uh, not yet.

01:02:06.848 --> 01:02:07.890
[sighs]

01:02:11.352 --> 01:02:12.186
[Myung-ju sighs]

01:02:19.068 --> 01:02:19.986
Oh…

01:02:25.074 --> 01:02:26.075
So…

01:02:27.368 --> 01:02:29.245
I have to go. Please forgive me.

01:02:30.371 --> 01:02:33.332
It's… I need to go and get my kids.

01:02:34.375 --> 01:02:36.627
Oh, that's fine. It's fine. Go.

01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:37.962
Yes, um, Miss Kim?

01:02:38.045 --> 01:02:42.175
If you could debrief with Mr. Cho
when he gets in,

01:02:42.258 --> 01:02:44.218
tell him I'll call
and give him more details.

01:02:44.302 --> 01:02:46.012
Okay. I got it.

01:02:46.888 --> 01:02:48.264
Thank you.

01:02:55.146 --> 01:02:56.147
[sighs]

01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:59.025
The director is in there being yelled at,

01:02:59.734 --> 01:03:01.819
and she heads out.

01:03:02.403 --> 01:03:04.280
She was the one that signed off
on the error

01:03:04.363 --> 01:03:06.866
but Director Jin chose not to report it
to the General Director.

01:03:12.497 --> 01:03:13.998
Where's Mrs. Oh?

01:03:15.124 --> 01:03:16.375
She had to go get her kids.

01:03:17.543 --> 01:03:20.213
Oh, I told her it was fine
to go get her kids.

01:03:22.048 --> 01:03:24.008
Oh, it is that time, I guess.

01:03:24.592 --> 01:03:26.093
So why don't we all head home?

01:03:26.177 --> 01:03:27.303
- Sure.
- Yeah.

01:03:47.490 --> 01:03:49.534
Don't delay. You make your choice,
and tell them right away.

01:03:49.617 --> 01:03:52.078
They're gonna be out there
for at least a month or two.

01:03:55.039 --> 01:03:57.041
[somber music playing]

01:04:05.299 --> 01:04:07.301
[indistinct chatter]

01:04:47.174 --> 01:04:48.342
Penny for your thoughts?

01:04:49.385 --> 01:04:50.386
Hm?

01:04:50.970 --> 01:04:52.096
I don't have any.

01:04:52.179 --> 01:04:54.348
Well, you seemed off
ever since you came back

01:04:54.432 --> 01:04:56.475
from the General Director's office.

01:04:56.559 --> 01:04:58.895
Oh, it's the typhoon center.

01:05:00.646 --> 01:05:02.607
Since the typhoons will be starting soon,

01:05:02.690 --> 01:05:05.776
I have to send someone from the team
to Jeju Island.

01:05:05.860 --> 01:05:07.236
Oh.

01:05:14.744 --> 01:05:15.745
Could you do it?

01:05:20.124 --> 01:05:21.542
I'd like it if you'd go.

01:05:39.644 --> 01:05:41.228
We need some time apart.

01:05:44.523 --> 01:05:46.442
What are… What's this about?

01:05:49.236 --> 01:05:50.613
We both need space.

01:05:52.406 --> 01:05:54.408
I think it's important for both of us.

01:05:55.660 --> 01:05:56.577
Yu-jin.

01:05:56.661 --> 01:06:01.207
We should take some time to think
how we can make this work.

01:06:03.167 --> 01:06:05.544
You know you need it as much as I do.

01:06:15.972 --> 01:06:17.264
Are you kidding me?

01:06:18.432 --> 01:06:20.685
All decisions I make at work
are taken seriously.

01:06:26.482 --> 01:06:27.858
So that means…

01:06:28.776 --> 01:06:30.945
you've given this considerable thought.

01:06:32.905 --> 01:06:35.533
Mm-hm. If it's all right with you.

01:06:47.712 --> 01:06:48.963
Is this about

01:06:49.672 --> 01:06:51.590
what you were saying earlier today?

01:06:52.258 --> 01:06:55.094
I think anyone else would have
assumed the same thing.

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.887
Even you, if you were in my shoes.

01:06:56.971 --> 01:06:58.222
No way.

01:06:58.305 --> 01:07:00.641
I would have wanted to hear
what you had to say.

01:07:03.644 --> 01:07:04.895
So, you're saying…

01:07:05.563 --> 01:07:07.398
you're going to leave me right now?

01:07:07.481 --> 01:07:09.191
I just need some space to breathe.

01:07:09.275 --> 01:07:11.485
Every time I see you frown
when you're at home,

01:07:11.569 --> 01:07:13.279
I think it's my fault.

01:07:13.362 --> 01:07:14.989
And I don't deserve to feel like that.

01:07:15.823 --> 01:07:17.742
When have I ever said you make me unhappy?

01:07:17.825 --> 01:07:20.786
Well, you do, in small ways,
like you don't wanna listen.

01:07:22.204 --> 01:07:25.374
It's exhausting to live with someone
that doesn't understand you.

01:07:26.292 --> 01:07:28.419
And you do?
Do you even understand me at all?

01:07:29.962 --> 01:07:33.466
Don't you know how much I love you?
I left the woman I dated for a decade.

01:07:33.549 --> 01:07:36.010
Can you stop saying how you abandoned
someone after ten years?

01:07:37.595 --> 01:07:39.513
I feel awful about that!

01:07:39.597 --> 01:07:42.099
I don't get how you don't think
I love you after that.

01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:45.102
You don't wanna register our marriage,
you're scared of the future…

01:07:45.186 --> 01:07:46.520
Exactly!

01:07:47.938 --> 01:07:51.108
So I think we should take some time
to figure things out.

01:07:53.360 --> 01:07:55.738
Think of what's best for us
and for each other.

01:08:00.701 --> 01:08:01.702
[sighs]

01:08:07.958 --> 01:08:11.128
[Si-woo] A blizzard of thoughts
swirls in my head these nights.

01:08:15.257 --> 01:08:16.550
[sighs]

01:08:18.094 --> 01:08:20.179
[Ki-jun] Ha-kyung
doesn't just date anybody,

01:08:20.262 --> 01:08:22.056
unless there's a chance of marriage.

01:08:22.139 --> 01:08:23.891
You are aware of that, right?

01:08:24.475 --> 01:08:26.185
If you don't wind up getting married,

01:08:26.268 --> 01:08:30.815
how do you know when you've reached
the height of your love?

01:08:30.898 --> 01:08:35.402
[breathes heavily]

01:08:37.822 --> 01:08:39.782
[Si-woo] When I have
too many thoughts at once,

01:08:39.865 --> 01:08:41.867
my heart gets confused.

01:08:42.743 --> 01:08:46.831
And a confused heart can only bring more

01:08:48.124 --> 01:08:52.545
and more and more thoughts.

01:08:58.217 --> 01:09:00.386
[somber music playing]

01:09:28.998 --> 01:09:31.417
[Si-woo] And our sleepless,
warm nights go on.

01:09:31.500 --> 01:09:33.627
The thoughts keep swirling.

01:09:36.172 --> 01:09:38.174
[somber music continues]

01:10:03.824 --> 01:10:05.201
[Ki-jun] If you leave me right now,

01:10:05.284 --> 01:10:06.702
it's really over between us.

01:10:06.785 --> 01:10:08.412
Are you sure you've thought this through?

01:10:08.495 --> 01:10:10.664
- Who's going to the typhoon center?
- I'm going, sir, it's me.

01:10:10.748 --> 01:10:14.126
I know you want to draw clear lines
between the KMA, me, work, and dating.

01:10:14.210 --> 01:10:17.504
[Si-woo] You compare me to him every time,
and it really bothers me.

01:10:17.588 --> 01:10:20.007
[Ha-kyung] I want things
to work out between us.

01:10:20.090 --> 01:10:23.177
Why do you keep confusing me
by changing your stance?

01:10:24.386 --> 01:10:26.013
- [coughs]
- [employee] Someone, please help!

01:10:26.096 --> 01:10:27.848
A student collapsed over here!

01:10:27.932 --> 01:10:29.642
- [siren wailing]
- What? An accident?

01:10:30.517 --> 01:10:31.852
[Yu-jin] Lee Si-woo.

01:10:31.936 --> 01:10:33.437
He works at the KMA.
